act = {"start": "2026-10-31 09:00", "end": "2026-10-31 10:20", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "Little Fugitive", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/little-fugitive-rd37", "blurb": "Seen through the eyes of a seven-year-old, Little Fugitive captures the excitement, fear and freedom of childhood in 1950s New York.\nWhen Joey runs away to Coney Island after being tricked into believing he has killed his brother, the legendary amusement park becomes a world of adventure and discovery. Co-directed by photographer Ruth Orkin, Morris Engel and Ray Ashley, this pioneering independent film’s handheld camerawork and naturalistic style would inspire the French New Wave."}
act = {"start": "2026-10-31 12:00", "end": "2026-10-31 13:26", "stage": "Everyman Cinema Screen 4", "act": "Into the Jaws of the Ogre", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/into-the-jaws-of-the-ogre-fw2q", "blurb": "Iranian filmmaker Mahsa Karampour tries to reconnect with her younger brother in this thoughtful, tender documentary road movie.\nTravelling across the US with Siavash, a punk musician exiled from their homeland, she tries to understand the life he has built far from her own. Moving between their journey and memories of childhood in Tehran, Karampour traces the distance that has grown between them, exploring siblinghood and the different ways we carry home with us.\nContains discussions of violence and murder, and themes of trauma."}
