act = {"start": "2026-10-31 13:15", "end": "2026-10-31 15:00", "stage": "Vue in the Light, Screen 11", "act": "DOTD: Never After Dark", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/never-after-dark-tmqc", "blurb": "A travelling medium uncovers dark, threatening secrets in this spine-chilling ghost story.\nAiri helps lost souls cross over to the afterlife. Arriving at a remote location, she encounters a spirit that will only come out at night and that refuses to leave. With no other option, Airi breaks her own rules to try and understand the spirit’s strange behaviour and immediately puts herself in danger. Dave Boyle’s masterful storytelling gives us a fresh and terrifying take on the haunted house genre.\nComtains scenes with strong bloody violence and gore."}
act = {"start": "2026-10-31 13:30", "end": "2026-10-31 15:08", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "Love Letter", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/love-letter-5wln", "blurb": "The directorial debut of the great Japanese actress and filmmaker Kinuyo Tanaka, who made 15 films with director Kenji Mizoguchi, Love Letter is a vivid evocation of post-war Tokyo a year after the American occupation ended.\nThe film follows repatriated veteran Reikichi, who searches for his lost love while translating romantic letters from Japanese women to American GIs. The film is a nuanced and perceptive romantic drama with a deft critique of patriarchal hypocrisy."}
