act = {"start": "2026-11-03 20:30", "end": "2026-11-03 21:59", "stage": "Everyman Cinema Screen 4", "act": "Yorkshire Short Film Competition", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/yorkshire-short-film-competition-nvjf", "blurb": "A defiant history of Bradford's 1in12 Club, the member-owned venue that became a beacon for protest and punk subcultures throughout the '80s and '90s. Long-standing club members reflect on the victories, struggles and the evolving destiny of the collective. Yorkshire Premiere | Michael McCabe | UK | 2025 | 13 mins | English\nA struggling tenant wants to escape his Pay-As-You-Go Life Tariff, but must first confront a relentlessly cheerful Customer Support officer conducting a routine “Life Utility Check-Up”. A Kafka-esque comedy set in a world where everything is chargeable. Yorkshire Premiere | Tom Diffenthal | UK | 2026 | 10 mins | English\nO love! O achin’ love! In this perfect blend of emo and romance, Helena (a teen with a heavy case of the “morbs”) struggles to navigate her first romance when various obstacles get in the way of her beloved Bernard and his many odes to her beauty. Laura Jayne Hodkin | UK | 2025 | 3 mins | English\nPerfectly fitting the remit of our Yorkshire Competition to support young filmmakers, this film confronts, with increasing absurdity, societal expectations of female self-surveillance and judgement, in a humorous, surreal short exploring teenage body-image. Yorkshire Premiere | Ava Bounds | UK | 2025 | 7 mins | English\nWhen a sudden and unexplained extinction wipes out Whitby’s lobster stocks, the local community is thrown into crisis. Fishermen and scientists must join forces to restore an ecosystem on the brink, with a little help from their hard-shelled heroes. World Premiere | Mikey Sneddon | UK | 2026 | 13 mins | English\nThis dark drama highlights the pressures of girlhood through Bailey, with big, beautiful lashes and very little confidence, a rebellious teen who is led astray by 