act = {"start": "2026-11-05 11:15", "end": "2026-11-05 12:46", "stage": "Everyman Cinema Screen 4", "act": "Louis le Prince International Short Film Competition 1", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/louis-le-prince-international-short-film-competition-1-85cs", "blurb": "A pop-up techno club in Amman. Inside, Jana’s fresh start is being challenged. Outside, Hasan quietly swallows heartbreak. They are two strangers on opposite sides of the street. A mesmerising portrait of loneliness, longing and resilience in a city in flux. Yorkshire Premiere | Yassmina Karajah | Canada, Jordan | 2025 | 21 mins | Arabic\nA tooth extraction introduces a watchful child to his mother’s new love. In Milk, tenderness turns grotesque, ordinary gestures uncanny, and love unfolds as a tale equal parts sweet and unsettling. International Premiere | Filippo Marasco | Italy | 2026 | 18 mins | Italian\n12-year-old Dadá sets off with her younger brother Tato to deliver a chicken to a local restaurant. But when she discovers Tato's close bond with the chicken, the journey becomes an awakening to vegetarianism,  violence, and the power of imaginative play. English Premiere | João Victor Silva, Matheus Malburg | Brazil | 2026 | 14 mins | Portuguese\nA dream of an enigmatic light triggers disappearances, leaving behind glowing human silhouettes. Hazy and experimental, the tale is witnessed in an eden-like allotment garden, where non-human witnesses and rumours of a healer from Mauritius deepen the mystery. International Premiere | Pauline Pichard | Switzerland | 2026 | 13 mins | French\nWhen German-Indonesian Yanto returns to Yogyakarta from Berlin, he finds his younger sister belongs more effortlessly than he does. Equally hilarious and heartbreaking, this sharp episodic portrait of mixed-race identity captures the ache of in-betweenness. Yorkshire Premiere | Berthold Wahjudi | Germany, Indonesia | 2026 | 25 mins | English, German, Indonesian"}
act = {"start": "2026-11-05 14:00", "end": "2026-11-05 15:23", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 2", "act": "Like a Fortress", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/like-a-fortress-64pb", "blurb": "In this raw and deeply intimate film, Lou Colpé turns the camera on her own experience of grief following the sudden loss of her partner.\nReturning to the home they shared, she finds refuge in its familiar spaces as life quietly continues around her. Told through on-screen text and gentle observations of friends, objects and changing seasons, this moving, diaristic documentary transforms the house into a sanctuary of memory and survival.\nContains themes of death and grief."}
