act = {"start": "2026-11-05 20:15", "end": "2026-11-05 21:51", "stage": "Vue in the Light, Screen 7", "act": "Bagworm", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/bagworm-8n1s", "blurb": "A surreal and darkly comic debut shot on 16mm about a man facing an existential meltdown that may have been caused by stepping on a rusty nail.\nCarroll is a paranoid, sexually frustrated hammer salesman who is convinced the world is coming to an end. When he accidentally steps on a rusty nail, his life starts to spiral in increasingly unhinged ways as he questions whether the universe really has it out for him or whether it’s all just grotesque hallucinations caused by this putrid infection."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-06 11:00", "end": "2026-11-06 12:29", "stage": "Everyman Cinema Screen 4", "act": "Louis le Prince International Short Film Competition 4", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/louis-le-prince-international-short-film-competition-4-c6t1", "blurb": "After a haunting planetarium visit, a young girl’s fascination with the Sun turns into an obsession with existence and its limits. In experimental black and white, childhood fears and realisations become a deeply relatable journey from wonder to sudden maturity. UK Premiere | Sofia Poncini | Argentina | 2025 | 9 mins | Spanish\nAmor, 67, keeps her fading parlor afloat while caring for her grandson. When a senior beauty pageant pops up, she sees a chance to feel seen again. A tender portrait of shedding insecurities and coming of age in a society obssessed with youth. World Premiere | Kylechandler Bigay | Philippines | 2026 | 21 mins | Tagalog\nIt's New Year’s Eve and Cleo and Tobias have a steamy relationship, yet things quickly become icy when they become locked out in the cold. Will they find the key they're searching for to enter back into the warmth? Yorkshire Premiere | Malin Barr | Sweden | 2026 | 15 mins | Norwegian, Swedish\nDuring a sudden downpour, a backpacker becomes stranded on an island. When she is offered shelter by a passing rickshaw driver, they share a fleeting yet profound moment of connection, overcoming the language barrier between them. International Premiere | Chilam Chan | China | 2025 | 16 mins | Mandarin Chinese\nIn 1994 Rwanda, days before the start of the genocide against Tutsi people, 10 year-old Jeanne searches for her pet goat while her parents worry about the future. On her quest, she is exposed to new realities casting doubt on the world she thought she knew. English Premiere | Aime Octave Ishimwe | Belgium | 2025 | 17 mins | Kinyarwanda\nBagchi is a dish antenna. Ganguly is a reverse camera. Pimple is a microwave. In a small, crumbling Indian town, three retirees refuse to be replaced by machines. In fact, they are on a mission to replace them. The new digital resistance begins. Yorkshire Premiere | Pranav Bhasin | India | 2026 | 11 mins | English, Hindi"}
act = {"start": "2026-11-06 11:15", "end": "2026-11-06 12:58", "stage": "Vue in the Light, Screen 12", "act": "Six Months in a Pink and Blue Building", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/six-months-in-a-pink-and-blue-building-bgwd", "blurb": "A boundless creative energy informs this warm and colourful family drama set in Mexico City in the early 90s.\nThe film begins as Bruno turns 11, and he struggles to come to terms with his own emerging sexuality as feelings for his best friend Vladimir grow. His confusion is compounded by the shock announcement that his father has HIV. But his bustling household is full of life, art, food and music. Thirty years later, Bruno revisits his memories and tries to come to terms with his past."}
