act = {"start": "2026-11-07 16:15", "end": "2026-11-07 17:46", "stage": "Everyman Cinema Screen 4", "act": "The Little Girl Who Sold the Sun + Le Franc", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/the-little-girl-who-sold-the-sun-le-franc-fvyq", "blurb": "Two extraordinary films from Senegalese master Djibril Diop Mambéty offer richly textured portraits of Dakar, where hardship coexists with possibility.\nIn The Little Girl Who Sold the Sun, Lissa Baléra is unforgettable as Sili, the city’s only female newspaper seller. Paired with Le Franc, a sly tale of a musician and a winning lottery ticket, these luminous, inventive films form Mambéty’s unfinished Tales of Ordinary People series and offer a glimpse of his singular vision.\nContains themes of poverty and discrimination."}
