act = {"start": "2026-11-13 17:30", "end": "2026-11-13 19:34", "stage": "Vue in the Light, Screen 11", "act": "The Beirut Trilogy", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/the-beirut-trilogy-nk8f", "blurb": "Presented together in their recent restorations, Jocelyne Saab’s landmark Beirut Trilogy forms a powerful, deeply personal record of a city transformed by war.\nMade between 1976 and 1982, these remarkable essay films follow Saab through the streets of her changing hometown, capturing displacement and everyday life amid destruction. Combining documentary images with poetic, sometimes epistolary narration, they form an intimate portrait of a disappearing city and of the people who persist.\nContains images of war, violence and destruction, and themes of death and displacement."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-13 18:00", "end": "2026-11-13 19:47", "stage": "Vue in the Light, Screen 7", "act": "Black Church Bay", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/black-church-bay-5zsn", "blurb": "Acclaimed for his short films - Pale Saint screened in the British short film competition at LIFF 2019 - writer-director Rhys Marc Jones has made a striking debut feature with Black Church Bay, a gripping and thought-provoking mystery thriller.\nIn a Welsh fishing village, deputy head teacher Barry (Tom Cullen) starts an affair with one of his students Jasper (Joe Locke). One night, Jasper mysteriously disappears, and Barry’s closely guarded secret threatens to come to light.\nContains scenes with nudity and sex."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-13 23:00", "end": "2026-11-14 00:31", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "NOTD: No Way Down", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/no-way-down-ythl", "blurb": "Five friends must find their way out of an abandoned tower in this tense horror-thriller.\nSet to get to the bottom of the urban legend born out of a string of mysterious disappearances in the sealed tower of a local housing project, a group of friends embark on a night expedition inside the building. They’re soon chased by something or someone who has no intention of letting them out alive, and as they try and find a way out, every door opened is a new terror awaiting them."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-13 23:00", "end": "2026-11-14 00:27", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "NOTD: Infirmary", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/infirmary-19gr", "blurb": "The found footage genre meets liminal space horror in Nicholas Pineda's tense and unnerving Infirmary.\nOn his first shift as a night watchmen, former soldier, Edward encounters increasingly strange phenomena alongside his coworker, retired police officer, Lester. As the unlikely partners navigate the empty halls of an old psychiatric hospital, seemingly unnatural events begin to occur that reveal not only the secrets of the building's past, but of the men themselves."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-13 23:00", "end": "2026-11-14 00:25", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "NOTD: From Beyond", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/from-beyond-79j8", "blurb": "Celebrating its 40th anniversary, Stuart Gordon's From Beyond reunites the director with his Re-animator stars, Jeffrey Combs and Barbara Crampton for another tale of Lovecraftian body-horror.\nDr. Edward Pretorius' Resonator machine has pierced the boundaries of reality as we know it and released unimaginable horrors. It falls to his assistant Dr. Crawford Tillinghast as well as disbelieving psychologist Dr. Katherine McMichaels to stop Pretorius' machine before it is too late."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-13 23:00", "end": "2026-11-14 00:31", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "NOTD: Oddities", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/oddities-sq42", "blurb": "A mixture of thriller and horror with touches of comedy, featuring a magnificent Adrienne Barbeau claiming her reign as horror queen.\nWhen two self-destructive best friends accidentally kill their drug dealer, they have to flee town. Stopping at a roadside antique shop, they quickly discover that the older woman running the place isn’t as sweet as she seems. It’s out of the frying pan and into the fire as they fight for survival while the criminals they were running away from descend on the property…"}
act = {"start": "2026-11-14 13:00", "end": "2026-11-14 14:52", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "Conversation with the Sea", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/conversation-with-the-sea-4cc3", "blurb": "Conversation with the Sea is a slow burning family drama about regret and reconciliation.\nSet in Jerusalem, the film follows Kamal, a 60-year-old Palestinian man, who is ordered by an Israeli court to pay a large social security debt allegedly owed by his son Wael. But Wael drowned in the Red Sea decades ago. When no official record of his death can be found, Kamal follows the only remaining lead to uncover what happened. Presented in partnership with the Leeds Palestinian Film Festival.\nContains racist language and scenes of violence."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-14 15:45", "end": "2026-11-14 18:34", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "Los Angeles Plays Itself", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/los-angeles-plays-itself-z754", "blurb": "A rare chance to see Thom Andersen’s landmark essay film, an extraordinary exploration of how cinema has represented and misrepresented its own hometown.\nDrawing on more than 200 film clips, Andersen unpicks the myths Hollywood has created around Los Angeles, revealing the histories and communities they have obscured. Monumental yet endlessly engrossing, Los Angeles Plays Itself is a dazzling portrait of a city built on storytelling and one of cinema’s great works of film criticism.\nContains scenes of violence, nudity, sexual content and drug use, and strong language."}
act = {"start": "2026-11-15 13:30", "end": "2026-11-15 15:10", "stage": "Hyde Park Picture House, Screen 1", "act": "Once Upon a Time in Harlem", "type": "film", "url": "https://www.leedsfilm.com/whats-on/once-upon-a-time-in-harlem-ynyl", "blurb": "This documentary time capsule is a glorious love letter to African-American cultural movement the Harlem Renaissance, filmed by legendary filmmaker William Greaves in 1972 and completed 50 years later by his son David.\nOnce Upon a Time in Harlem offers audiences a unique chance to hang out with a lively gathering of artists, musicians and academics at Duke Ellington’s townhouse. An essential work that is a distinctive and poetic snapshot of a moment in time and the sharing of knowledge and creativity.\nContains racist attitudes and language."}
